course: dictionary
lesson: 12007
title: Small sounds: cheep
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cheep is a short, high, weak sound. Young birds make it, often when they are hungry or waiting for their mum. Say it out loud: cheep.
explain: «The baby birds cheeped in the nest, waiting for food.» The clues are baby birds, nest and waiting for food, so cheeped must mean made a short, high sound. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The baby birds made a short, high sound in the nest" still makes sense.
explain: Cheep can be a verb (to cheep) or a noun (a cheep): «The chick gave a tiny cheep.» People also say, «Not a cheep out of you!» Here cheep means any sound at all, so it means be completely quiet.
explain: Other words are close in meaning: chirp, tweet, peep and chirrup. They are all sounds made by birds, so when you meet one, check the sentence to see which one fits best.
fact: «Cheep» means a short, high, weak sound made by a young bird.
fact: «Cheep» can be a verb (to cheep) or a noun (a cheep).
fact: «Not a cheep» is an informal phrase meaning not a single sound.
fact: Similar sound words include chirp, tweet, peep and chirrup.
fact: Use context to check: if the sentence is about a nest or baby birds, cheep is likely to fit.
exercise: «The chick gave a tiny cheep from the nest.» What is a cheep? | A kind of nest | A big splash in the pond | *A short, high, weak sound | A long, deep song
exercise: «The class went quiet. Not a cheep out of anyone.» What does not a cheep mean? | Everyone cheered loudly | *Not a single sound | A bird flew away | Everyone began to sing
exercise: Find and copy one word from this list that is a similar sound word. | sleep | nest | castle | *chirp
test: «The baby birds cheeped for food.» Which word means the same as cheeped? | Flew very fast | Fell asleep | Grew very tall | *Made a short, high, weak sound
test: Which is the past tense of cheep? | cheeping | cheeps | cheepy | *cheeped
exam: Mum says, «Not a cheep!» in a quiet room. What does she want? | A nest for the baby birds | *Complete silence, no sound at all | A bird song for the class | Loud singing
